{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And if his means do not reach.</b> Since one who became impure by entering the Temple and one who swears an oath of expression do not derive benefit from the sin, the verse was lenient upon them with the offering of וירד. But one who eats fat and blood, one who eats on Yom HaKippurim, one who does work on the Sabbath, and one who lies with a forbidden relative — who derive benefit from the sin — they have a fixed offering. All the more so one who worships idolatry unwittingly, who stretched out his hand against the foundation; and one who benefited from consecrated property, where there are two, that he benefited and swore falsely — likewise brings an asham for the silver of shekels."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:34.545064032Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}